. 
. * ===========================================================================
> ===
. * 1.1  IMPORT AND APPEND 72 MONTHLY CIG FILES
. * ===========================================================================
> ===
. * Each CIG file is one month of lot publications from ANAC. A "lot" (CIG) is 
> a
. * single procurement contract. The file has ~80 columns; we keep the ones we 
> need.
. *
. * WHY monthly files? ANAC publishes data in monthly batches. We use 2018–2023
. * (72 months = 72 files). 2016–2017 are blocked on the ANAC API.
. 
. di as text _n "========================================"

========================================

. di as text    "  1.1: IMPORTING CIG FILES"
  1.1: IMPORTING CIG FILES

. di as text    "========================================"
========================================

. 
. tempfile combined

. local first 1

. 
. forvalues y = 2018/2023 {
  2.     forvalues m = 1/12 {
  3.         local mm : display %02.0f `m'
  4.         local csvfile "data/raw/cig_csv_`y'_`mm'.csv"
  5. 
.         capture confirm file "`csvfile'"
  6.         if _rc {
  7.             di as error "  Missing: `csvfile' — skipping"
  8.             continue
  9.         }
 10. 
.         di as text "  Importing `csvfile' ..."
 11. 
.         * Import as all-string to avoid type mismatches across months
.         import delimited using "`csvfile'", delimiter(";") stringcols(_all) c
> lear
 12.         rename *, lower
 13. 
.         * Keep relevant columns. The full CIG file has ~80 columns; we only
.         * need: identifiers (cig, cig_accordo_quadro), contract descriptors
.         * (oggetto_principale_contratto = SERVIZI/FORNITURE/LAVORI, settore,
.         * importo_lotto = base value), dates, procedure type, geography,
.         * and the ESITO (outcome) columns the pilot originally missed.
.         capture {
 14.             keep cig cig_accordo_quadro oggetto_principale_contratto setto
> re ///
>                 importo_lotto data_pubblicazione data_scadenza_offerta ///
>                 cod_tipo_scelta_contraente tipo_scelta_contraente ///
>                 sezione_regionale cod_cpv codice_ausa ///
>                 cf_amministrazione_appaltante ///
>                 denominazione_amministrazione_ap ///
>                 anno_pubblicazione mese_pubblicazione ///
>                 stato luogo_istat provincia ///
>                 durata_prevista n_lotti_componenti ///
>                 flag_urgenza flag_delega ///
>                 flag_pnrr_pnc ///
>                 cod_esito esito data_comunicazione_esito ///
>                 cod_modalita_realizzazione modalita_realizzazione
 15.         }
 16.         * WHY "denominazione_amministrazione_ap"? The raw column
.         * DENOMINAZIONE_AMMINISTRAZIONE_APPALTANTE has 40 characters; Stata
.         * truncates variable names to 32, so after import it is called
.         * denominazione_amministrazione_ap (checked on all 72 headers).
.         * HISTORY (fixed 13 Nov 2026, Step 0 of adding the groupmate's outcom
> es;
.         * logged under Deviations): until then this list used the full 40-cha
> r
.         * name, so the keep failed in ALL 72 months and the fallback below al
> ways
.         * ran, losing 7 columns (data_scadenza_offerta, the authority name,
.         * durata_prevista, n_lotti_componenti, flag_delega,
.         * cod_modalita_realizzazione, modalita_realizzazione). No result used
.         * them. With the fix they are kept; the bid deadline (deadline_date, 
> 1.5)
.         * is needed for the deadline-to-award outcomes.
.         * Fall back to a minimal set if the full keep fails (should not happe
> n
.         * now; the log prints "Column mismatch" if it does).
.         if _rc {
 17.             di as error "  Column mismatch in `csvfile' — trying minimal s
> et"
 18.             describe, short
 19.             capture {
 20.                 keep cig cig_accordo_quadro oggetto_principale_contratto s
> ettore ///
>                     importo_lotto data_pubblicazione ///
>                     cod_tipo_scelta_contraente tipo_scelta_contraente ///
>                     sezione_regionale cod_cpv codice_ausa ///
>                     cf_amministrazione_appaltante ///
>                     anno_pubblicazione mese_pubblicazione ///
>                     stato luogo_istat provincia ///
>                     flag_urgenza flag_pnrr_pnc ///
>                     cod_esito esito data_comunicazione_esito
 21.             }
 22.             if _rc {
 23.                 di as error "  Still can't keep required columns — skippin
> g"
 24.                 continue
 25.             }
 26.         }
 27. 
.         * Short name for the authority's name. WHY rename? Later Parts merge 
> in
.         * the firm name (`denominazione`, 5.1); a distinct name avoids any
.         * confusion with Stata's variable-name abbreviations.
.         capture rename denominazione_amministrazione_ap authority_name
 28. 
.         * FILTER 1: Keep only SERVICES and SUPPLIES (our population of intere
> st).
.         * WHY? The €139k threshold applies specifically to services/supplies.
.         * Works (LAVORI) have a different threshold (€150k). Mixing them woul
> d
.         * contaminate the design.
.         keep if inlist(oggetto_principale_contratto, "SERVIZI", "FORNITURE")
 29. 
.         * FILTER 2: Keep only ORDINARY sectors.
.         * WHY? Special sectors (utilities: water, energy, transport, postal)
.         * have their own EU directives and different thresholds.
.         keep if settore == "SETTORI ORDINARI" | settore == "ORDINARI"
 30. 
.         gen int source_year = `y'
 31.         gen byte source_month = `m'
 32. 
.         if `first' {
 33.             save `combined', replace
 34.             local first 0
 35.         }
 36.         else {
 37.             append using `combined'
 38.             save `combined', replace
 39.         }
 40. 
.         di as text "    Kept " _N " cumulative rows"
 41.     }
 42. }
