. * ===========================================================================
> ===
. * 3.2  POLYNOMIAL BUNCHING ESTIMATOR AT €139k
. * ===========================================================================
> ===
. * METHOD (Kleven 2016):
. * 1. Create €1k bins in a wider window (€100k–€200k).
. * 2. Exclude bins in a "manipulation window" around the cutoff, (134k, 144k].
. * 3. Fit an order-7 polynomial to the bin counts OUTSIDE the excluded window.
. *    This gives a "counterfactual" density: what the distribution would look
. *    like without bunching.
. * 4. Compare actual vs counterfactual counts in the excluded window at or bel
> ow 139k.
. * 5. "Excess mass" = actual − counterfactual. Normalise by average counterfac
> tual
. *    bin count to get b_hat.
. *
. * b_hat tells us HOW MUCH extra mass there is below the cutoff, relative to
. * what we'd expect if authorities didn't manipulate lot values.
. 
. di as text _n "========================================"

========================================

. di as text    "  3.2: BUNCHING ESTIMATOR"
  3.2: BUNCHING ESTIMATOR

. di as text    "========================================"
========================================

. 
. local cutoff = 139000

. local bin_width = 1000

. local poly_order = 7

. local window_lo = 100000

. local window_hi = 200000

. local excl_lo = 5000

. local excl_hi = 5000

. 
. * Bins are (k−1000, k] — right-closed — so that a lot at exactly €139,000 fal
> ls
. * in the last bin BELOW the cutoff, (138k, 139k], consistent with the "≤ 139k
. * is eligible" definition (section 1.7). Round values (e.g. €140,000) then si
> t
. * at the TOP edge of their bin, hence the round-number dummies use bin_bunch 
> + 500.
. * The window is (100k, 200k]: with right-closed bins, ">= 100k" would create 
> a
. * first "bin" holding only lots at exactly €100,000 (a heap).
. gen bin_bunch = ceil(importo_lotto / `bin_width') * `bin_width' - `bin_width'
> /2 ///
>     if importo_lotto > `window_lo' & importo_lotto <= `window_hi'
(1,244,813 missing values generated)

. gen float bin_norm = (bin_bunch - `cutoff') / `bin_width'
(1,244,813 missing values generated)

. 
. foreach p of global GROUPS {
  2.     di as text _n "--- Bunching estimator: Period `p' ---"
  3. 
.     preserve
  4.     keep if ${g_`p'} & !missing(bin_bunch)
  5.     gen byte one = 1
  6.     collapse (sum) count=one, by(bin_bunch bin_norm)
  7. 
.     * Mark the excluded window (±5k around cutoff)
.     gen byte excluded = (bin_bunch >= (`cutoff' - `excl_lo') & bin_bunch < (`
> cutoff' + `excl_hi'))
  8. 
.     * Generate polynomial terms
.     forvalues j = 2/7 {
  9.         gen float bin_norm`j' = bin_norm^`j'
 10.     }
 11. 
.     * Round-number dummies (Chetty et al. 2011): multiples of 10k, and of 5k
.     * that are not multiples of 10k. WHY the 5k dummy? Lots heap at €105k,
.     * €115k, … and the €135k heap sits inside the excluded window just below
.     * the cutoff; without the dummy it is counted as bunching.
.     gen byte round10k = (mod(bin_bunch + 500, 10000) == 0)
 12.     gen byte round5k  = (mod(bin_bunch + 500, 5000) == 0) & !round10k
 13. 
.     * Fit polynomial on bins OUTSIDE the excluded window, with round-number d
> ummies
.     reg count bin_norm bin_norm2 bin_norm3 bin_norm4 bin_norm5 ///
>         bin_norm6 bin_norm7 round10k round5k if excluded == 0
 14.     predict counterfactual
 15. 
.     * Excess mass below cutoff
.     summarize count if bin_bunch >= (`cutoff' - `excl_lo') & bin_bunch < `cut
> off'
 16.     local actual_below = r(sum)
 17.     summarize counterfactual if bin_bunch >= (`cutoff' - `excl_lo') & bin_
> bunch < `cutoff'
 18.     local cf_below = r(sum)
 19. 
.     * Normalise by avg counterfactual at threshold (Kleven 2016 standard)
.     summarize counterfactual if bin_bunch >= (`cutoff' - `excl_lo') & bin_bun
> ch < `cutoff'
 20.     local avg_cf_threshold = r(mean)
 21. 
.     * Missing mass above cutoff
.     summarize count if bin_bunch >= `cutoff' & bin_bunch < (`cutoff' + `excl_
> hi')
 22.     local actual_above = r(sum)
 23.     summarize counterfactual if bin_bunch >= `cutoff' & bin_bunch < (`cuto
> ff' + `excl_hi')
 24.     local cf_above = r(sum)
 25.     local missing_above = `cf_above' - `actual_above'
 26. 
.     local excess_mass = `actual_below' - `cf_below'
 27.     local b_hat = `excess_mass' / `avg_cf_threshold'
 28. 
.     di as text "  Actual below (excl window): " %10.0f `actual_below'
 29.     di as text "  Counterfactual below:       " %10.0f `cf_below'
 30.     di as text "  Excess mass:                " %10.0f `excess_mass'
 31.     di as text "  Missing mass above:         " %10.0f `missing_above'
 32.     di as text "  Avg cf at threshold:        " %10.0f `avg_cf_threshold'
 33.     di as text "  >>> b_hat (`p'):           " %10.3f `b_hat'
 34. 
.     * Store b_hat for the P2 − control difference (3.4)
.     local b_hat_`p' = `b_hat'
 35. 
