. 
. * ---- 4.6a: Donut specifications ----
. * WHY? Lots exactly at the cutoff are most likely to be manipulated (bunching
> ).
. * Dropping lots within d of the cutoff removes the most manipulated observati
> ons.
. * If the effect SURVIVES (or strengthens), the results are not driven by bunc
> hing.
. 
. di as text _n "--- Donuts ---"

--- Donuts ---

. foreach d in 1000 2500 5000 {
  2.     local dk = `d'/1000
  3.     di as text _n "  Donut `dk'k:"
  4.     foreach var in days_award lratio single_bid {
  5.         capture reghdfe `var' i.below##i.post##c.x [aw=kw40] ///
>             if main_sample == 1 & abs(x) <= 40000 & abs(x) >= `d' & has_award
>  == 1, ///
>             absorb(cpv2_post region_post ym) vce(cluster authority_id)
  6.         if !_rc {
  7.             di as text "    `var': " %8.4f _b[1.below#1.post] ///
>                 " (" %7.4f _se[1.below#1.post] ")"
  8.             rpost Mrob donut`d' `var'
  9.         }
 10.     }
 11. }

